# GitHub-source installations

- When a GitHub source directory does not yet exist, shallow-clone only the latest commit into `~/.local/share/<application>` and retain the checkout there. GitHub-sourced MCP servers are the exception: use `~/.local/mcp/<server>`.
- On later runs, fetch and compare the checkout with its configured upstream before pulling updates.
- Build and install after the initial clone, and rebuild and reinstall only when the source revision changes.
